[{"text":"Overview.","anchor":"see-also","section":"See also"},{"text":"When you square an expression with dummy indices, you must rename them first. People often do this by hand, e.g. as in","anchor":"manipulations-of-tensorial-quantities","section":"Manipulations of tensorial quantities"},{"text":"ex1 = (FV[p, \\[Mu]] + FV[q, \\[Mu]]) FV[r, \\[Mu]] FV[r, \\[Nu]]","anchor":"cb1","section":"Manipulations of tensorial quantities"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{r}^{\\mu } \\overline{r}^{\\nu } \\left(\\overline{p}^{\\mu }+\\overline{q}^{\\mu }\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb1-1","section":"Manipulations of tensorial quantities"},{"text":"ex1 (ex1 /. \\[Mu] -> \\[Rho]) Contract[%]","anchor":"cb2","section":"Manipulations of tensorial quantities"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{r}^{\\mu } \\left(\\overline{r}^{\\nu }\\right)^2 \\overline{r}^{\\rho } \\left(\\overline{p}^{\\mu }+\\overline{q}^{\\mu }\\right) \\left(\\overline{p}^{\\rho }+\\overline{q}^{\\rho }\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb2-2","section":"Manipulations of tensorial quantities"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{r}^2 \\left(\\overline{p}\\cdot \\overline{r}+\\overline{q}\\cdot \\overline{r}\\right)^2\\]","anchor":"cb2-2","section":"Manipulations of tensorial quantities"},{"text":"However, FeynCalc offers a function for that","anchor":"cb2-2","section":"Manipulations of tensorial quantities"},{"text":"FCRenameDummyIndices[ex1]","anchor":"cb3","section":"Manipulations of tensorial quantities"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{r}^{\\nu } \\overline{r}^{\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$19})} \\left(\\overline{p}^{\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$19})}+\\overline{q}^{\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$19})}\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb3-1","section":"Manipulations of tensorial quantities"},{"text":"ex1 FCRenameDummyIndices[ex1] Contract[%]","anchor":"cb4","section":"Manipulations of tensorial quantities"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{r}^{\\mu } \\overline{r}^{\\nu } \\overline{r}^{\\nu } \\left(\\overline{p}^{\\mu }+\\overline{q}^{\\mu }\\right) \\overline{r}^{\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$20})} \\left(\\overline{p}^{\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$20})}+\\overline{q}^{\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$20})}\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb4-2","section":"Manipulations of tensorial quantities"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{r}^2 \\left(\\overline{p}\\cdot \\overline{r}+\\overline{q}\\cdot \\overline{r}\\right)^2\\]","anchor":"cb4-2","section":"Manipulations of tensorial quantities"},{"text":"Notice that FCRenameDummyIndices does not canonicalize the indices","anchor":"cb4-2","section":"Manipulations of tensorial quantities"},{"text":"FV[p, \\[Nu]] FV[q, \\[Nu]] - FV[p, \\[Mu]] FV[q, \\[Mu]] FCRenameDummyIndices[%]","anchor":"cb5","section":"Manipulations of tensorial quantities"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{p}^{\\nu } \\overline{q}^{\\nu }-\\overline{p}^{\\mu } \\overline{q}^{\\mu }\\]","anchor":"cb5-2","section":"Manipulations of tensorial quantities"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{p}^{\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$22})} \\overline{q}^{\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$22})}-\\overline{p}^{\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$21})} \\overline{q}^{\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$21})}\\]","anchor":"cb5-2","section":"Manipulations of tensorial quantities"},{"text":"There is a function for that too","anchor":"cb5-2","section":"Manipulations of tensorial quantities"},{"text":"FV[p, \\[Nu]] FV[q, \\[Nu]] - FV[p, \\[Mu]] FV[q, \\[Mu]] FCCanonicalizeDummyIndices[%]","anchor":"cb6","section":"Manipulations of tensorial quantities"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{p}^{\\nu } \\overline{q}^{\\nu }-\\overline{p}^{\\mu } \\overline{q}^{\\mu }\\]","anchor":"cb6-2","section":"Manipulations of tensorial quantities"},{"text":"\\[0\\]","anchor":"cb6-2","section":"Manipulations of tensorial quantities"},{"text":"Often we also need to uncontract already contracted indices. This is done by Uncontract. By default, it handles only contractions with Dirac matrices and Levi-Civita tensors","anchor":"cb6-2","section":"Manipulations of tensorial quantities"},{"text":"LC[][p, q, r, s] Uncontract[%, p] Uncontract[%%, p, q]","anchor":"cb7","section":"Manipulations of tensorial quantities"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\overline{p}\\overline{q}\\overline{r}\\overline{s}}\\]","anchor":"cb7-3","section":"Manipulations of tensorial quantities"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{p}^{\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$31})} \\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$31})\\overline{q}\\overline{r}\\overline{s}}\\]","anchor":"cb7-3","section":"Manipulations of tensorial quantities"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{p}^{\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$33})} \\overline{q}^{\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$32})} \\left(-\\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$32})\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$33})\\overline{r}\\overline{s}}\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb7-3","section":"Manipulations of tensorial quantities"},{"text":"SP[p, q] Uncontract[%, p]","anchor":"cb8","section":"Manipulations of tensorial quantities"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{p}\\cdot \\overline{q}\\]","anchor":"cb8-2","section":"Manipulations of tensorial quantities"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{p}\\cdot \\overline{q}\\]","anchor":"cb8-2","section":"Manipulations of tensorial quantities"},{"text":"To uncontract scalar products as well, use the option Pair->All","anchor":"cb8-2","section":"Manipulations of tensorial quantities"},{"text":"Uncontract[%, p, Pair -> All]","anchor":"cb9","section":"Manipulations of tensorial quantities"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{p}^{\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$34})} \\overline{q}^{\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$34})}\\]","anchor":"cb9-1","section":"Manipulations of tensorial quantities"}]